# Scope for release archives (git archive / GitHub's release source zip,
# which Zenodo pulls from via the GitHub-Zenodo integration). This does NOT
# affect what's tracked in git or what `git clone` checks out - only what
# ends up in the downloadable archive for a tagged release.
#
# Kept: code/, LICENSE, README.md, plus the 3 files actually needed for
# `renv::restore()` to reproduce the exact package versions on its own:
# .Rprofile (triggers it), renv/activate.R (the bootstrap script it calls),
# renv.lock (the package manifest). Everything else below is excluded,
# including renv/settings.json and renv/.gitignore - small, but not needed.

.github export-ignore
.gitattributes export-ignore
.gitignore export-ignore
.vscode export-ignore
*.Rproj export-ignore
*.code-workspace export-ignore
*.docx export-ignore
CLAUDE.md export-ignore
notes/ export-ignore
tests/ export-ignore
renv/* export-ignore
renv/activate.R -export-ignore
